msgid "Ce résultat est une pré-évaluation à caractère informatif. Il n’engage aucune autorité et ne préjuge d’aucune décision : seules les autorités compétentes décident."
msgstr ""
"This result is a preliminary assessment for information purposes. It binds "
"no authority and prejudges no decision: only the competent authorities "
"decide."

#: .\templates\documents\partials\register.html
msgid "L’état d’une pièce dit ce que le dossier a reçu, et rien de plus. Aucune ligne de ce registre ne vaut acceptation."
msgstr ""
"The status of a document says what the case file has received, and nothing "
"more. No row in this register amounts to acceptance."

#: .\templates\selection\identity.html
msgid "La personne a consenti à cette communication, pour l’objet et jusqu’à l’échéance indiqués ci-dessous. Chacune de vos consultations lui est visible."
msgstr ""
"The person has consented to this disclosure, for the purpose and until the "
"date indicated below. Each of your consultations is visible to them."

#: .\apps\accounts\middleware.py
msgid ""
"Votre rôle donne accès au dossier d’autres personnes : l’authentification "
"à deux facteurs (TOTP) doit être activée avant de continuer."
msgstr ""
"Your role gives access to the case files of other people: two-factor "
"authentication (TOTP) must be enabled before you continue."

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Candidata — contenuto ereditato"
msgstr "Candidate — inherited content"

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Chi ha aperto la fonte ufficiale quel giorno. Una data senza un nome non è una verifica."
msgstr ""
"Who opened the official source on that day. A date without a name is not a "
"verification."

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Chi ha approvato, come testo che sopravvive all'anonimizzazione dell'account. È questo campo, non la chiave esterna, che il vincolo di database esige: una regola in vigore deve dire chi la sostiene anche dopo che quell'account è sparito."
msgstr ""
"Who approved, as text that survives the anonymisation of the account. It is "
"this field, and not the foreign key, that the database constraint requires: "
"a rule in force must say who stands behind it even after that account has "
"gone."

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Da dove viene il testo della regola. Il contenuto ereditato parte da «candidata»."
msgstr ""
"Where the text of the rule comes from. Inherited content starts at "
"“candidate”."

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Derivata da un contenuto della piattaforma precedente"
msgstr "Derived from content of the previous platform"

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Fonte verificata"
msgstr "Source verified"

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Ordinamento da cui la fonte proviene: IT, EU, MA, o BIL per un atto bilaterale. Sta sulla fonte e non solo sulla regola, perché una regola italiana può poggiare su una direttiva europea, e chi rilegge deve vedere quale dei due è cambiato."
msgstr ""
"Legal system the source comes from: IT, EU, MA, or BIL for a bilateral "
"instrument. It sits on the source and not only on the rule, because an "
"Italian rule may rest on a European directive, and whoever re-reads it must "
"see which of the two has changed."

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Redatta dalla fonte normativa"
msgstr "Drafted from the legislative source"

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Ripresa dalla piattaforma precedente"
msgstr "Carried over from the previous platform"

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "Una regola approvata o in vigore deve dire chi la sostiene. Passare da «%(status)s» attraverso il flusso di revisione, non cambiando lo stato a mano."
msgstr ""
"A rule that is approved or in force must say who stands behind it. Pass "
"through “%(status)s” by way of the review workflow, not by changing the "
"status by hand."

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "approvata da (registrato)"
msgstr "approved by (recorded)"

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "provenienza del contenuto"
msgstr "provenance of the content"

#: .\apps\rules\models.py
msgid "verificata da"
msgstr "verified by"

#: .\apps\rules\services.py
msgid "Fonti ancora da verificare alla fonte ufficiale: %(list)s. Servono data, nome di chi ha verificato, e URL o autorità."
msgstr ""
"Sources still to be verified against the official source: %(list)s. A date, "
"the name of whoever verified them, and a URL or authority are required."

#: .\apps\rules\services.py
msgid "Non si verifica la fonte di una regola che non ne ha nessuna."
msgstr "The source of a rule that has none cannot be verified."

#: .\apps\rules\services.py
msgid "Una regola non entra in vigore senza un approvatore registrato."
msgstr "A rule does not come into force without a recorded approver."

#: .\templates\cases\assessment.html
msgid "Les règles qui ont produit ce résultat n’ont été approuvées par aucun juriste : elles ont été mises en vigueur pour montrer le fonctionnement de la plateforme. Les dates de consultation affichées plus bas ne correspondent à aucune vérification à la source officielle. Ce résultat ne doit servir à aucune démarche."
msgstr ""
"The rules that produced this result have not been approved by any lawyer: "
"they were brought into force to show how the platform works. The "
"consultation dates shown further down correspond to no verification against "
"the official source. This result must not be used for any administrative "
"step."

#: .\templates\cases\assessment.html
